  "problem": "The vertical velocity of the eagle increases at a rate proportional to the square of the time $t.$ In addition, the eagle loses $2\\,\\text{m/s}$ in the positive $y$-direction due to wind resistance. It is known that the eagle's vertical velocity equals $2\\,\\text{m}/\\text{s}$ when $t=2\\,\\text{s}.$\n\nThe differential equation that describes the eagle's vertical velocity is ${y}^{′}(t)=$\n{{field-1}}.",
